      "tree": {
        "sha": "fe4fea8a23983a2b8b982e8508035efbcb4676f3",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/trees/fe4fea8a23983a2b8b982e8508035efbcb4676f3"
      },
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree fe4fea8a23983a2b8b982e8508035efbcb4676f3\nparent 9bf4815b94b9eaf8807f4e569091778da6c338d5\nauthor optout21 <13562139+optout21@users.noreply.github.com> 1793622707 +0100\ncommitter optout21 <13562139+optout21@users.noreply.github.com> 1794500049 +0100\n\ntest: p2p: check v1 magic bytes only after the full header\n\nThe v1 message parser in P2PConnection rejected the stream as soon as\nthe first 4 bytes did not match the network magic. bitcoind's\nV1Transport::readHeader waits for the full 24-byte header before\nchecking the magic.\n\nThe v2 to v1 downgrade relies on bitcoind's behaviour: an outbound v2\nconnection is only retried with v1 (V2Transport::ShouldReconnectV1)\nif at least a v1 header's worth of bytes had been sent before the\npeer disconnected. If the node's first send reaches the test peer in\nsmall pieces, the Python peer could disconnect after just 4 bytes, the\nnode would not retry with v1, and p2p_v2_encrypted.py would time out\nwaiting for the reconnection.\n\nMatch bitcoind by checking the magic only once the full header has\nbeen received.\n",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQGzBAABCgAdFiEEmuHXOVRjWiwQgEZAHancOgcdFYIFAmr15hIACgkQHancOgcd\nFYISrAwAjhTHmzimBg6aFbaB1xRz3jg0dGSQ/FNphhaVZaBDpOjSvHNyifgu2/Q+\n4ZH92Y8oTYFjmFmPmOlujV9FzNWJtXkPtJJub0XmREu3RhvVwEznAMazc4sTMkwv\njaNE9dt5QRoMDcLZx4uQ72SIcPtlUUK8ivYTnHjDb7IxJdHxxSpPQXN4PZjdrJDc\npHV/QerWNUrpn1RstcgPPCGjKmuCRcoeL8vB/K13flnxkpTkFx0BIHBTAztK3hy7\n5QoUx2/zmZrUPO/3hPpQ/grDIdRGIYdFKnIEQVV1maRJ0eWnsQ8KZrkAjB/BxrFI\ne+mC3Metu2i5gWl3hOdU79YMwLPuESjahCKzslBREJW1usdUbID5nBcNh3ZalsYl\nD9kTMNGB/ghuDkiceq5jottE0+kVWPEBBvCVBN+rw1nOwY4mCDSMM/Yg4pUw9X1B\nw4xggrkhCC7mYxQUsEnoRyrL8n2my+fzVj6272Hurqip+vR5WPVXA08UlcbzdxAg\nrBANa1HS\n=kHd+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----"
