        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/trees/56df0ab3dcbfa62ffef1d3a37ff31c32edb46c51"
      },
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree 56df0ab3dcbfa62ffef1d3a37ff31c32edb46c51\nparent be35cbb0b16d97e82f5634e76314e87b430a9360\nauthor optout21 <13562139+optout21@users.noreply.github.com> 1794488213 +0100\ncommitter optout21 <13562139+optout21@users.noreply.github.com> 1794500102 +0100\n\ntest: p2p_v2_misbehaving: Handle partial ellswift read\n\nThe node's 64-byte ellswift key can arrive in several chunks. In that\ncase EncryptedP2PState.complete_handshake() returns (0, b\"\") to signal\nthat more data is needed. The WrongGarbageTerminatorState override\nbit-flipped the returned bytes unconditionally, which crashed in\nrandom_bitflip() on empty input and dropped the connection.\n\nReturn the \"need more data\" result unchanged before tampering with it.\n",
