      "body": "crACK be88a3b926bd18d2243ca1a2e21332bca4f5d7e1\n\nReviewed the logic; both changes correctly handle partial reads in the test framework:\n\n- `test_framework/p2p.py`: deferring the v1 magic-bytes check until the full 24-byte header has arrived matches `V1Transport`, which only validates the header after reading all of it. Checked that nothing relies on the old early-raise: `p2p_invalid_messages.py:test_magic_bytes` drives the wrong-magic case from the sender side and asserts the *node* disconnects (`Wrong MessageStart` in the debug log), so it never depends on the harness raising at 4 bytes; the `recvbuf[:4] == magic_bytes` check in `p2p_private_broadcast_retry_v1.py` is a separate v1/v2-determination path and is unaffected.\n- `p2p_v2_misbehaving.py`: guarding the empty `handshake_bytes` return before `random_bitflip(handshake_bytes[:16])` correctly propagates the \"not all 64 ellswift bytes received yet\" signal instead of bitflipping an empty slice.\n",
